<h1 style="font-size: 18pt; color: #e21833; font-weight: bold; font-family: Verdana; margin: 20px 0 5px; border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd; padding-bottom: 4px;">Workday Procurement: Non-Catalog Orders</h1>
<div style="background-color: #f9f9f9; padding: 10px 16px; border-radius: 4px; margin-bottom: 25px; font-size: 11pt; text-align: center; border: 1px solid #eee;"><a style="color: #0056b3; text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;" href="#overview" rel="nofollow">Overview</a> | <a style="color: #0056b3; text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;" href="#completion" rel="nofollow">Completion of the REQ</a> | <a style="color: #0056b3; text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;" href="#after" rel="nofollow">Post-Submission Steps</a></div>
<h2 id="overview" style="font-size: 14pt; color: #454545; font-weight: bold; font-family: Verdana; margin: 24px 0 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd; padding-bottom: 4px;">Overview</h2>
<p style="margin-bottom: 15pt;">The <strong>Non-Catalog Order</strong> protocol applies to transactions involving <strong>any supplier</strong> that does not maintain an active integration link within Shell Shop but remains formally registered inside Workday. If your chosen vendor is completely omitted from the Workday directory database, they must submit comprehensive supplier request onboarding documents prior to logging a standard requisition workflow. Share this onboarding portal link with new vendors to initiate the registration phase: <a style="color: #0056b3;" href="https://rhs.umd.edu/WDsupplier" rel="nofollow">https://rhs.umd.edu/WDsupplier</a></p>
<div style="background-color: #fcf8e3; border-left: 4px solid #f0ad4e; padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 4px; margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6;"><strong style="color: #a94442; display: block; margin-bottom: 10pt; font-size: 12pt;">Note: Labor Cost Configuration for Capital Assets</strong>
<p style="margin: 0 0 10pt 0;">When a Capital Asset and Labor/Installation is included on the requisition, calculate the specific labor cost allocation using the following formula sequence:</p>
<div style="background-color: #fff; padding: 12px 16px; border: 1px solid #e0e0e0; border-radius: 4px; font-family: monospace; font-size: 10pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; color: #444;">1. [Capital Asset Amount] x 100 = [Base Multiplier]<br>2. [Base Multiplier] &divide; [Total Labor/Installation Amount] = [Factor]<br>3. [Factor] x 100 = <strong>Labor Cost Allocation</strong></div>
<strong style="color: #242424; display: block; margin-bottom: 4px;">Example:</strong>
<p style="margin: 0 0 10pt 0; font-family: monospace; background-color: #fff; padding: 8px 12px; border: 1px solid #eee; border-radius: 4px; display: inline-block;">$5,200 (CA) x 100 = 520,000 &divide; $33,000 (L) = 15.7575 x 100 = <strong>$1,575.00</strong></p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-style: italic; color: #555;">*This calculated amount represents the labor cost for the individual Capital Asset. It must be entered as a distinct line item on the REQ and subsequently subtracted from the gross total of the primary Installation/Labor line item. Under <strong>"Review Required"&nbsp;</strong>use&nbsp;<strong>"Modify System or Asset"</strong>, and in the memo of this line item, note the description of the Capital Asset for labor cost.</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-style: italic; color: #555;">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-style: italic; color: #555;"><em>** Subtract all individual labor cost entries from the total cost of the Installation/Labor line item.</em></p>
</div>
<div style="background-color: #fafafa; padding: 16px 20px; border-left: 4px solid #454545; border-radius: 4px; margin-bottom: 20px;"><strong style="color: #242424; font-size: 11pt; display: block; margin-bottom: 10pt;">Required Procurement Resource Libraries</strong>
<ul style="padding-left: 20px; margin: 0; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 11pt;">
<li style="margin-bottom: 6px;"><strong>Smith IT Procurement Catalog (ServiceNow):</strong> <a style="color: #0056b3;" href="https://rhs.umd.edu/procurement" rel="nofollow">https://rhs.umd.edu/procurement</a><br><span style="color: #666;">Used to log purchases and upload critical transaction documents.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 6px;"><strong>Workday Purchases Tracker (Google Sheets):</strong> <a style="color: #0056b3;" href="https://rhs.umd.edu/wdpurchase" rel="nofollow">https://rhs.umd.edu/wdpurchase</a><br><span style="color: #666;">Centralized log for all orders submitted through Workday.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 0;"><strong>Procurement Codes Reference Chart (Google Sheets):</strong> <a style="color: #0056b3;" href="https://rhs.umd.edu/pcodes" rel="nofollow">https://rhs.umd.edu/pcodes</a><br><span style="color: #666;">Contains Commodity Codes, Spend/Object Codes, USource Department Numbers, and F&amp;A Business Manager assignments.</span></li>
</ul>
</div>
